    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0579" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/830: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-28T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:26 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. English translation of previous note of acceptance withdrawn and new
                    substitute note received. The number and date are the same, and with the
                    deletion of the phrase “adjusted by the Government <pb facs="0580" n="460"
                        xml:id="pg460"/> of the United States” the phraseology of the two notes is
                    exactly the same.</p>
                <p>I believe that the Peruvian Government would be gratified if neither note were
                    published, and if possible I urge that their wishes be respected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
